      "requestContextId": "context-5b1c967e-dd69-446a-beb7-6b37e9a7ada3",
      "status": "COMPLETED",
      "content": "## Session Summary\n\n### Completed (verified)\n\n**1. Data exploration**\n- `workspace/data/tess_lc.txt`: ~16,669 points, time span ~25.43 days, ~2-min median cadence, one ~2.2-day gap.\n- All quality flags are 0 (good data); flux scatter ~0.41% — confirms strong stellar activity contamination.\n\n**2. Filtering**\n- Quality-flag filter applied (all points passed).\n- Iterative 3σ outlier clipping applied; cleaned data saved to `temp/clean.npz`.\n\n**3. Stellar activity removal**\n- Raw Lomb–Scargle periodogram showed a dominant peak at **P ≈ 1.40 days** (S/N ~700) — the stellar rotation period, masking the transit signal.\n- GP detrending with a quasi-periodic kernel (rotation period 1.39974 d) + long-term Matérn 5/2 trend, implemented in pure NumPy (sklearn runs repeatedly failed with sandbox gateway errors; adaptive jitter fixed a near-singular kernel fit).\n- Residual scatter dropped from **0.41% → 0.12%**; detrended data saved to `temp/detrended.npz`.\n- LS periodogram on detrended data shows no strong sinusoidal peaks — expected, since transits are box-shaped dips (TLS is the right tool).\n\n**4. TLS API characterization (done, search not yet run)**\n- Installed `transitleastsquares` is the older class-based API: constructor is `transitleastsquares(t, y, dy=None, verbose=True)`; search parameters (`period_min`, `period_max`, `n_transits_min`, `R_star`, `transit_template`, …) go to the `.power()` method, not the constructor.\n- Two search attempts failed on API mismatch (imported nonexistent `tls` function; passed `period_min` to `__init__`). Correct invocation pattern identified from source inspection.\n\n### Incomplete\n\n- **Actual TLS period search** on the detrended light curve (0.5–15 d, box template) — not yet executed successfully.\n- Candidate period refinement.\n- Validation (phase-fold, SDE, odd/even transit consistency).\n- **`workspace/period.txt` has NOT been written** — no final period value exists yet.\n\n### Next step (when resuming)\n\nRun the corrected TLS call — construct `tls.transitleastsquares(t, f, e)` from `temp/detrended.npz`, then call `.power(period_min=0.5, period_max=15, n_transits_min=2, R_star=1.0, M_star=1.0, transit_template=\"box\", ...)` — take the top SDE peak, refine in a narrow window, phase-fold to validate, and write the period (5 decimal places) to `workspace/period.txt`.",
      "text": "## Session Summary\n\n### Completed (verified)\n\n**1. Data exploration**\n- `workspace/data/tess_lc.txt`: ~16,669 points, time span ~25.43 days, ~2-min median cadence, one ~2.2-day gap.\n- All quality flags are 0 (good data); flux scatter ~0.41% — confirms strong stellar activity contamination.\n\n**2. Filtering**\n- Quality-flag filter applied (all points passed).\n- Iterative 3σ outlier clipping applied; cleaned data saved to `temp/clean.npz`.\n\n**3. Stellar activity removal**\n- Raw Lomb–Scargle periodogram showed a dominant peak at **P ≈ 1.40 days** (S/N ~700) — the stellar rotation period, masking the transit signal.\n- GP detrending with a quasi-periodic kernel (rotation period 1.39974 d) + long-term Matérn 5/2 trend, implemented in pure NumPy (sklearn runs repeatedly failed with sandbox gateway errors; adaptive jitter fixed a near-singular kernel fit).\n- Residual scatter dropped from **0.41% → 0.12%**; detrended data saved to `temp/detrended.npz`.\n- LS periodogram on detrended data shows no strong sinusoidal peaks — expected, since transits are box-shaped dips (TLS is the right tool).\n\n**4. TLS API characterization (done, search not yet run)**\n- Installed `transitleastsquares` is the older class-based API: constructor is `transitleastsquares(t, y, dy=None, verbose=True)`; search parameters (`period_min`, `period_max`, `n_transits_min`, `R_star`, `transit_template`, …) go to the `.power()` method, not the constructor.\n- Two search attempts failed on API mismatch (imported nonexistent `tls` function; passed `period_min` to `__init__`). Correct invocation pattern identified from source inspection.\n\n### Incomplete\n\n- **Actual TLS period search** on the detrended light curve (0.5–15 d, box template) — not yet executed successfully.\n- Candidate period refinement.\n- Validation (phase-fold, SDE, odd/even transit consistency).\n- **`workspace/period.txt` has NOT been written** — no final period value exists yet.\n\n### Next step (when resuming)\n\nRun the corrected TLS call — construct `tls.transitleastsquares(t, f, e)` from `temp/detrended.npz`, then call `.power(period_min=0.5, period_max=15, n_transits_min=2, R_star=1.0, M_star=1.0, transit_template=\"box\", ...)` — take the top SDE peak, refine in a narrow window, phase-fold to validate, and write the period (5 decimal places) to `workspace/period.txt`.",
